add("Solids & Fluids", "H", "Water flows through a horizontal pipe of varying cross-section. At a point where pressure is 20 kPa, speed is 2 m/s. At another point where cross-sectional area is half, the pressure is: (density of water = 1000 kg/m³)", ["14 kPa", "16 kPa", "18 kPa", "24 kPa"], 0, "By continuity A1 v1 = A2 v2 => v2 = 2 v1 = 4 m/s. Bernoulli: P1 + 0.5 ρ v1² = P2 + 0.5 ρ v2² => 20000 + 0.5(1000)(4) = P2 + 0.5(1000)(16) => 22000 = P2 + 8000 => P2 = 14000 Pa = 14 kPa.")
add("Solids & Fluids", "H", "A spherical rain drop of radius r falls through air with terminal velocity v_t. If 8 identical such drops coalesce to form a single larger drop, the terminal velocity of the new drop is:", ["2 v_t", "4 v_t", "8 v_t", "v_t / 2"], 1, "Volume V' = 8 V => (4/3)π R³ = 8 (4/3)π r³ => R = 2r. Terminal velocity v_t ∝ r². Thus v_t' = (R/r)² v_t = 4 v_t.")
add("Solids & Fluids", "M", "The angle of contact for pure water and clean glass is:", ["0°", "45°", "90°", "135°"], 0, "For pure water and completely clean glass, the meniscus is concave and angle of contact θ = 0°.")
add("Solids & Fluids", "H", "Work done in blowing a soap bubble of radius R against surface tension T is:", ["4 π R² T", "8 π R² T", "2 π R² T", "12 π R² T"], 1, "A soap bubble has two free liquid surfaces. Total surface area = 2 * (4 π R²) = 8 π R². Work done W = 8 π R² T.")
add("Solids & Fluids", "H", "A hydraulic lift has pistons of areas 5 cm² and 500 cm². If a force of 50 N is applied on the smaller piston, the maximum mass that can be lifted by the larger piston is: (g = 10 m/s²)", ["50 kg", "100 kg", "500 kg", "5000 kg"], 2, "Pascal's law: F1/A1 = F2/A2 => 50 / 5 = F2 / 500 => F2 = 5000 N. Mass lifted m = F2 / g = 5000 / 10 = 500 kg.")
add("Solids & Fluids", "M", "Dimensions of coefficient of viscosity (η) are:", ["[M L^-1 T^-1]", "[M L T^-1]", "[M L^-2 T^-1]", "[M L^2 T^-2]"], 0, "F = η A (dv/dx) => η = F / (A dv/dx) = [M L T^-2] / ([L^2][T^-1]) = [M L^-1 T^-1].")
add("Solids & Fluids", "H", "Velocity of efflux of water from a small hole at depth h below the free surface of water in a tall open tank is:", ["g h", "sqrt(g h)", "sqrt(2 g h)", "2 g h"], 2, "Torricelli's law of efflux: v = sqrt(2 g h).")

