# Current Electricity (P151-P160)
add("Current Electricity", "M", "A wire of resistance 12 Ω is stretched to double its initial length. Its new resistance will be:", ["12 Ω", "24 Ω", "36 Ω", "48 Ω"], 3, "When stretched to double length (L' = 2L), area halves (A' = A/2). New resistance R' = ρ (2L)/(A/2) = 4 R = 4 * 12 = 48 Ω.")
add("Current Electricity", "H", "A battery of EMF 12 V and internal resistance 2 Ω is connected to a 10 Ω external resistor. Terminal potential difference across the battery is:", ["10 V", "12 V", "2 V", "8 V"], 0, "Current I = E / (R + r) = 12 / (10 + 2) = 1 A. Terminal voltage V = E - I r = 12 - (1 * 2) = 10 V.")
add("Current Electricity", "M", "Three identical resistors of 6 Ω each are connected in parallel. Equivalent resistance of the combination is:", ["2 Ω", "6 Ω", "18 Ω", "0.5 Ω"], 0, "1/R_eq = 1/6 + 1/6 + 1/6 = 3/6 = 1/2 => R_eq = 2 Ω.")
add("Current Electricity", "H", "In a Wheatstone bridge circuit, four arm resistances are P = 10 Ω, Q = 20 Ω, R = 15 Ω, S = 30 Ω. The bridge is:", ["Unbalanced", "Balanced", "Short-circuited", "Open-circuited"], 1, "Balance condition P / Q = R / S => 10 / 20 = 15 / 30 = 0.5. Bridge is perfectly balanced.")
add("Current Electricity", "H", "A 100 W, 220 V bulb and a 50 W, 220 V bulb are connected in series across a 220 V supply. Power consumed by 50 W bulb is approximately:", ["11.1 W", "22.2 W", "33.3 W", "50 W"], 1, "R = V²/P. R1 (100W) = 484 Ω, R2 (50W) = 968 Ω. Total R = 1452 Ω. Current I = 220 / 1452 = 0.1515 A. Power in R2 = I² R2 = (0.1515)² * 968 ≈ 22.2 W.")
add("Current Electricity", "M", "Kirchhoff's First Law (Junction Rule) ∑ I = 0 is based on the law of conservation of:", ["Energy", "Charge", "Momentum", "Mass"], 1, "Junction rule states total current entering a node equals total current leaving, expressing Conservation of Charge.")
add("Current Electricity", "H", "A wire of resistance R is cut into 5 equal parts. These 5 parts are then connected in parallel. Equivalent resistance of combination is:", ["R / 5", "R / 10", "R / 25", "5 R"], 2, "Each part has resistance r = R / 5. Connected in parallel: 1/R_eq = 5 * (1 / (R/5)) = 25 / R => R_eq = R / 25.")
add("Current Electricity", "H", "Potentiometer wire of length 10 m has resistance 20 Ω. It is connected in series with a 3V battery and 10 Ω resistor. Potential gradient along wire is:", ["0.1 V/m", "0.2 V/m", "0.3 V/m", "0.5 V/m"], 1, "Current I = 3 / (20 + 10) = 0.1 A. Voltage across 10m wire V = I * R_wire = 0.1 * 20 = 2 V. Potential gradient k = V / L = 2 / 10 = 0.2 V/m.")
add("Current Electricity", "M", "Drift velocity of free electrons in a copper conductor is of the order of:", ["10^8 m/s", "3 x 10^8 m/s", "10^-4 m/s", "10^2 m/s"], 2, "Drift velocity of conduction electrons under typical electrical fields is very small, ~10^-4 m/s (fraction of a mm/s).")
add("Current Electricity", "H", "Temperature coefficient of resistance α of a wire is 0.004 /°C. If resistance is 10 Ω at 0°C, its resistance at 100°C will be:", ["10.4 Ω", "14 Ω", "40 Ω", "140 Ω"], 1, "R_T = R_0 (1 + α ΔT) = 10 (1 + 0.004 * 100) = 10 (1 + 0.4) = 14 Ω.")

# Magnetism (P161-P170)
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "H", "A proton (q = 1.6 x 10^-19 C, m = 1.67 x 10^-27 kg) enters a uniform magnetic field B = 0.5 T perpendicularly with velocity v = 2 x 10^6 m/s. Radius of circular path is:", ["2.09 cm", "4.18 cm", "8.35 cm", "10.5 cm"], 1, "r = m v / (q B) = (1.67 x 10^-27 * 2 x 10^6) / (1.616 x 10^-19 * 0.5) = (3.34 x 10^-21) / (0.8 x 10^-19) = 0.04175 m = 4.18 cm.")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "M", "Magnetic field at the center of a circular coil of radius R carrying current I is:", ["μ0 I / (2 R)", "μ0 I / (4 π R)", "μ0 I / (2 π R)", "μ0 I R / 2"], 0, "B = μ0 I / (2 R) by Biot-Savart law at coil center.")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "H", "Two long parallel straight wires carrying currents of 10 A and 20 A in the same direction are separated by 0.2 m. Force per unit length between them is:", ["2 x 10^-4 N/m (attractive)", "4 x 10^-4 N/m (attractive)", "2 x 10^-4 N/m (repulsive)", "4 x 10^-4 N/m (repulsive)"], 0, "F/L = (μ0 I1 I2) / (2 π d) = (4π x 10^-7 * 10 * 20) / (2 π * 0.2) = (2 x 10^-7 * 200) / 0.2 = 2 x 10^-4 N/m. Same direction currents ATTRACT.")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "M", "Magnetic force on a charge q moving with velocity v in a magnetic field B is zero when angle θ between v and B is:", ["0° or 180°", "45°", "90°", "270°"], 0, "F = q v B sin θ = 0 when sin θ = 0, i.e. θ = 0° (parallel) or 180° (anti-parallel).")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "H", "A solenoid of length 0.5 m has 500 turns and carries a current of 2 A. Magnetic field inside the solenoid is: (μ0 = 4π x 10^-7 T·m/A)", ["2.51 x 10^-3 T", "1.25 x 10^-3 T", "5.02 x 10^-3 T", "2.51 x 10^-4 T"], 0, "n = N / L = 500 / 0.5 = 1000 turns/m. B = μ0 n I = 4π x 10^-7 * 1000 * 2 = 8π x 10^-4 = 2.51 x 10^-3 T.")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "H", "A galvanometer of resistance 50 Ω gives full scale deflection for 1 mA. To convert it into a voltmeter reading up to 10 V, series resistance required is:", ["9950 Ω", "10000 Ω", "9900 Ω", "10050 Ω"], 0, "V = I_g (G + R) => 10 = 0.001 (50 + R) => 10000 = 50 + R => R = 9950 Ω.")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "M", "Work done by a magnetic field on a moving point charge is:", ["Always positive", "Always negative", "Always zero", "Depends on charge sign"], 2, "Magnetic force F = q(v x B) is always perpendicular to velocity v (F ⊥ v), so work W = F . v dt = 0.")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "H", "Cyclotron frequency of a charged particle in a magnetic field B is independent of:", ["Speed of particle", "Charge of particle", "Magnetic field B", "Mass of particle"], 0, "Cyclotron frequency f = q B / (2 π m). It depends on q, B, m but is completely independent of particle speed v or orbit radius r.")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "M", "Unit of magnetic flux density B is Tesla (T). 1 Tesla is equal to:", ["1 Weber / m²", "1 Weber · m²", "1 Newton / A", "1 Joule / C"], 0, "Magnetic flux Φ = B A => B = Φ / A = 1 Wb/m² = 1 Tesla.")
add("Moving Charges & Magnetism", "H", "A circular loop of radius 0.1 m carrying current 5 A is placed in a uniform magnetic field 0.2 T. Maximum torque experienced by the loop is:", ["0.0314 N·m", "0.314 N·m", "0.0628 N·m", "0.628 N·m"], 0, "Area A = π r² = 3.1416 * 0.01 = 0.031416 m². Magnetic moment M = I A = 5 * 0.031416 = 0.157 A·m². Max torque τ = M B = 0.157 * 0.2 = 0.0314 N·m.")

