add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "M", "Lenz's law of electromagnetic induction is a consequence of the law of conservation of:", ["Charge", "Mass", "Energy", "Momentum"], 2, "Lenz's law ensures mechanical work done against opposing induced EMF is converted into electrical energy, satisfying Energy Conservation.")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "H", "A metal rod of length 1 m is rotated at 10 rad/s about one end perpendicular to a magnetic field B = 0.4 T. Induced EMF across the ends is:", ["1 V", "2 V", "4 V", "8 V"], 1, "Induced EMF ε = 0.5 B L² ω = 0.5 * 0.4 * (1²) * 10 = 2 V.")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "M", "Self-inductance of a coil is 5 H. If current through it changes from 4 A to 0 A in 0.1 s, induced EMF in coil is:", ["50 V", "100 V", "200 V", "500 V"], 2, "ε = - L (dI/dt) = - 5 * (0 - 4)/0.1 = 5 * 40 = 200 V.")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "H", "Energy stored in a 2 H inductor carrying a steady current of 4 A is:", ["8 J", "16 J", "32 J", "64 J"], 1, "U = 0.5 L I² = 0.5 * 2 * (4²) = 16 J.")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "H", "A square loop of side 0.2 m is placed perpendicular to a magnetic field B changing at a rate dB/dt = 10 T/s. Induced EMF in loop is:", ["0.1 V", "0.4 V", "0.8 V", "4.0 V"], 1, "ε = dΦ/dt = A (dB/dt) = (0.2 * 0.2) * 10 = 0.04 * 10 = 0.4 V.")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "M", "Dimensions of self-inductance L are:", ["[M L² T^-2 A^-2]", "[M L² T^-2 A^-1]", "[M L T^-2 A^-2]", "[M L² T^-1 A^-2]"], 0, "U = 0.5 L I² => L = 2U / I² = [M L² T^-2] / [A²] = [M L² T^-2 A^-2].")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "H", "A aircraft with wingspan 40 m flies horizontally at 250 m/s in a region where vertical component of Earth's magnetic field is 3 x 10^-5 T. EMF induced between wingtips is:", ["0.3 V", "0.6 V", "1.2 V", "3.0 V"], 0, "ε = B_v L v = (3 x 10^-5) * 40 * 250 = 3 x 10^-5 * 10000 = 0.3 V.")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "H", "Two coaxial coils have mutual inductance M = 0.05 H. If current in primary coil changes as I = 10 sin(100 π t) A, maximum induced EMF in secondary coil is:", ["15.7 V", "50 π V", "157 V", "50 V"], 2, "ε_2 = - M (dI/dt) = - 0.05 * (10 * 100 π cos(100 π t)) = - 50 π cos(100 π t). Max magnitude = 50 π = 50 * 3.1416 = 157 V.")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "M", "Eddy currents produced in solid metal blocks inside changing magnetic fields can be minimized by:", ["Using solid copper blocks", "Laminating the iron core", "Increasing magnetic field frequency", "Using non-magnetic metals"], 1, "Laminating iron cores into thin insulated sheets breaks eddy current loops, reducing Joule heating losses.")
add("Electromagnetic Induction (EMI)", "H", "SI unit of Henry (H) is equivalent to:", ["Weber / Ampere", "Volt · second / Ampere", "Joule / Ampere²", "All of the above"], 3, "L = Φ/I (Wb/A), ε = L dI/dt (V·s/A), U = 0.5 L I² (J/A²). All three units are equivalent to 1 Henry.")

# AC (P181-P190)
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "M", "An AC voltage source is given by V = 220 √2 sin(100 π t) V. Its RMS voltage and frequency are:", ["220 V, 50 Hz", "220 V, 100 Hz", "311 V, 50 Hz", "220 √2 V, 50 Hz"], 0, "V_0 = 220 √2 => V_rms = V_0 / √2 = 220 V. Angular frequency ω = 100 π => 2 π f = 100 π => f = 50 Hz.")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "H", "A series LCR circuit has R = 30 Ω, X_L = 80 Ω, and X_C = 40 Ω connected to 200V RMS AC supply. Impedance Z and current I are:", ["50 Ω, 4 A", "70 Ω, 2.85 A", "50 Ω, 2 A", "30 Ω, 6.67 A"], 0, "Z = √(R² + (X_L - X_C)²) = √(30² + (80 - 40)²) = √(900 + 1600) = √2500 = 50 Ω. Current I = V / Z = 200 / 50 = 4 A.")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "M", "In a purely inductive AC circuit, phase relationship between voltage V and current I is:", ["V and I in phase", "V leads I by 90°", "I leads V by 90°", "V leads I by 180°"], 1, "In pure inductor, voltage leads current by 90° (π/2 radians).")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "H", "Resonance frequency of a series LCR circuit with L = 0.1 H and C = 10 μF is:", ["159.2 Hz", "318.3 Hz", "500 Hz", "1000 Hz"], 0, "f_0 = 1 / (2 π √(L C)) = 1 / (2 π √(0.1 * 10^-5)) = 1 / (2 π √(10^-6)) = 1000 / (2 π) = 159.2 Hz.")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "H", "Power factor of a series LCR circuit at resonance is:", ["0", "0.5", "0.707", "1.0"], 3, "At resonance X_L = X_C => Z = R. Power factor cos φ = R / Z = R / R = 1.0.")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "M", "Inductive reactance X_L of a 0.2 H inductor connected to 50 Hz AC supply is:", ["10 π Ω", "20 π Ω", "50 π Ω", "100 π Ω"], 1, "X_L = 2 π f L = 2 * π * 50 * 0.2 = 20 π Ω ≈ 62.8 Ω.")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "H", "Ideal step-up transformer has primary to secondary turn ratio N_p : N_s = 1 : 10. If primary voltage is 220 V and primary current is 5 A, secondary voltage and current are:", ["2200 V, 0.5 A", "22 V, 50 A", "2200 V, 50 A", "22 V, 0.5 A"], 0, "V_s = V_p (N_s/N_p) = 220 * 10 = 2200 V. For ideal transformer P_p = P_s => V_p I_p = V_s I_s => I_s = 5 / 10 = 0.5 A.")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "H", "Average power consumed in a pure capacitor connected to AC supply over one complete cycle is:", ["0.5 C V²", "C V² f", "Zero", "V² / X_C"], 2, "In pure capacitor phase angle φ = 90°. Power factor cos 90° = 0 => Average power P_avg = V_rms I_rms cos 90° = 0.")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "M", "Q-factor (Quality factor) of a series resonant LCR circuit is given by:", ["(1 / R) √(L / C)", "R √(L / C)", "(1 / R) √(C / L)", "R √(C / L)"], 0, "Q = ω_0 L / R = (1 / R) √(L / C).")
add("Alternating Current (AC)", "H", "In an AC circuit, peak current I_0 = 5 A. The RMS current is:", ["2.5 A", "3.535 A", "5 A", "7.07 A"], 1, "I_rms = I_0 / √2 = 5 / 1.414 = 3.535 A.")

